  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> be two points on the parabola, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></math> and let <math><mi>X</mi></math> be any point on the arc <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>O</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> of this parabola, where <math><mi>O</mi></math> is the vertex of this parabola, such that the area of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> is maximum. Then this maximum area (in sq. units) is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Gob8q",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>625</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>",
